---This API resource represents the vulnerability report for a specified Compute Engine virtual machine (VM) instance at a given point in time. For more information, see [Vulnerability reports](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/instances/os-inventory-management#vulnerability-reports).
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReport
---@field vulnerabilities? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityList Output only. List of vulnerabilities affecting the VM.
---@field highestUpgradableCveSeverity? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportHighestUpgradableCveSeverityEnum Output only. Highest level of severity among all the upgradable vulnerabilities with CVEs attached.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp for when the last vulnerability report was generated for the VM.
---@field name? string Output only. The `vulnerabilityReport` API resource name. Format: `projects/{project_number}/locations/{location}/instances/{instance_id}/vulnerabilityReport`

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportHighestUpgradableCveSeverityEnum "VULNERABILITY_SEVERITY_LEVEL_UNSPECIFIED"|"NONE"|"MINIMAL"|"LOW"|"MEDIUM"|"HIGH"|"CRITICAL"

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReport[]

---A vulnerability affecting the VM instance.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerability
---@field details? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetails Contains metadata as per the upstream feed of the operating system and NVD.
---@field updateTime? string The timestamp for when the vulnerability was last modified.
---@field items? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItemList List of items affected by the vulnerability.
---@field createTime? string The timestamp for when the vulnerability was first detected.
---@field availableInventoryItemIds? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.StringList Corresponds to the `AVAILABLE_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. If there is no available fix, the field is empty. The `inventory_item` value specifies the latest `SoftwarePackage` available to the VM that fixes the vulnerability.
---@field installedInventoryItemIds? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.StringList Corresponds to the `INSTALLED_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. This field displays the inventory items affected by this vulnerability. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. For some distros, this field may be empty.

---Contains metadata information for the vulnerability. This information is collected from the upstream feed of the operating system.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetails
---@field severity? string Assigned severity/impact ranking from the distro.
---@field description? string The note or description describing the vulnerability from the distro.
---@field cve? string The CVE of the vulnerability. CVE cannot be empty and the combination of should be unique across vulnerabilities for a VM.
---@field cvssV2Score? number The CVSS V2 score of this vulnerability. CVSS V2 score is on a scale of 0 - 10 where 0 indicates low severity and 10 indicates high severity.
---@field references? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReferenceList Corresponds to the references attached to the `VulnerabilityDetails`.
---@field cvssV3? gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.CVSSv3 The full description of the CVSSv3 for this vulnerability from NVD.

---A reference for this vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReference
---@field source? string The source of the reference e.g. NVD.
---@field url? string The url of the reference.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReferenceList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityDetailsReference[]

---OS inventory item that is affected by a vulnerability or fixed as a result of a vulnerability.
---@class gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItem
---@field upstreamFix? string The upstream OS patch, packages or KB that fixes the vulnerability.
---@field availableInventoryItemId? string Corresponds to the `AVAILABLE_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. If there is no available fix, the field is empty. The `inventory_item` value specifies the latest `SoftwarePackage` available to the VM that fixes the vulnerability.
---@field fixedCpeUri? string The recommended [CPE URI](https://cpe.mitre.org/specification/) update that contains a fix for this vulnerability.
---@field installedInventoryItemId? string Corresponds to the `INSTALLED_PACKAGE` inventory item on the VM. This field displays the inventory items affected by this vulnerability. If the vulnerability report was not updated after the VM inventory update, these values might not display in VM inventory. For some operating systems, this field might be empty.

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItemList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityItem[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerabilityList gcp.unstable.osconfig_v1alpha.VulnerabilityReportVulnerability[]

